The first substantive gap is already visible: the spec has no universal end-to-end claim equating the function’s result with the reference stable ordering; its universal entry claim stops at the semantics’ own `sortWith` term, while the `sortWith`/`specSort` claims cover only empty and singleton cases. I’ll still complete every required stage, including independent execution, a clean proof run, exhaustive rule accounting, and a fresh false mutation.
